<!-- DOD:END -->

## Description

The DETECT step of this bundle's uniform loop (detect → setup → verify), and a `kind:state` task — idempotent,
so re-running it is part of Repair. Detection is the load-bearing primitive: it is what makes re-runs safe and
collapses install / update / repair into one workflow.

1. **Read** this task's prior receipt entry (keyed by `step:detect`) — understand what a previous pass found and
   why, not just a status flag.
2. **Inspect** the environment for ⟨what "present" means for `{{bundle-id}}` — the tool/binary/config/registration
   this bundle delivers⟩. Reason against the acceptance criterion; the intent may be met by a different
   mechanism than this recipe names, or a partial prior attempt may need reconciling.
3. If the intent is **already satisfied**, RECORD that (and how you determined it) and let `{{bundle-id}}-2`
   skip its work. Otherwise, hand off to `{{bundle-id}}-2` to set it up.

Detection records what is true *now* by looking; it never assumes the recipe's prior runs reflect current
reality. A pure-detection pass that places nothing has no reversible effect — where that is genuinely the case
the executor may opt this task out of the recording defaults — but if detection adopts or marks anything, record
it. Never reach into another bundle's state.
